, then always stop and remove the server. Exercise default/contextual paths, profiles, optional imports, and fail-fast behavior. Use a test-local truststore if TLS-specific coverage is attempted.\n  \n  Risks:\n  - The upstream quick start uses HTTPS and generated certificates; HTTP dev mode will not cover TLS behavior.\n  - Tests require a working Docker daemon and reliable container cleanup.\n  \n  Iteration progress:\n  - Iteration: 1/3\n  - Overall coverage: 0/2\n  \n  Full dynamic-access coverage report, all classes with uncovered call sites:\n  ### org.springframework.cloud.vault.config.VaultConfigDataLoader\n  Source: /home/mihailo/git/graalvm-reachability-metadata-copy/forge/local_repositories/source_context/org.springframework.cloud/spring-cloud-vault-config/5.0.2/main/extracted/org/springframework/cloud/vault/config/VaultConfigDataLoader.java\n  Coverage: 0/2\n  Uncovered call sites:\n  - [reflection] java.lang.reflect.Field#set(java.lang.Object, java.lang.Object) <- org.springframework.cloud.vault.config.VaultConfigDataLoader.lambda$reconfigureLogger$0(VaultConfigDataLoader.java:415) (line 415)\n  - [reflection] java.lang.reflect.Field#set(java.lang.Object, java.lang.Object) <- org.springframework.cloud.vault.config.VaultConfigDataLoader.lambda$reconfigureLogger$1(VaultConfigDataLoader.java:424) (line 424)\n  \n  \n  Rules (test contract: §root/FS-test-contract):\n  - Add or refine tests so execution reaches as many of the uncovered call sites as possible, across all classes listed above. Be pragmatic — focus on the most straightforward call sites first and keep the generation concise. §root/FS-test-contract.3.1\n  - After finishing this generation, create a git commit with a focused message describing the test changes.\n[recv] prompt success\n[recv] {\"type\": \"agent_start\"}\n[recv] {\"type\": \"turn_start\"}\n[recv] {\"type\": \"message_start\", \"message\": {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Role: You are an expert JV